    <string name="info_battery_time_title">About Battery Time</string>
    <string name="info_battery_time_body">Estimated time until your battery is empty, based on your current charge level and how much power your phone is using right now. Real usage varies — opening a game or turning on GPS will shorten this, screen-off idle will lengthen it.\n\nOn devices that don\'t expose a working battery fuel gauge (including most Samsung phones), this estimate isn\'t available and the card shows only your last-full-charge time instead.</string>

    <string name="info_thermal_title">About Thermal</string>
    <string name="info_thermal_body">Android reports a \"thermal state\" based on how hot the phone\'s CPU and battery are. When things get hot, Android slows the phone down to protect itself — that\'s what this card reflects.\n\nNominal: no throttling.\nLight / Moderate / Severe: Android is progressively reducing performance.\nCritical and above: the phone may shut down to cool off.</string>

    <string name="info_network_title">About Network Usage</string>
    <string name="info_network_body">Your mobile data usage for the current billing cycle, compared to the plan limit you set. Wi-Fi is tracked separately and doesn\'t count against your plan.\n\nThe cycle start date matters — if you set it wrong, the numbers won\'t match your carrier\'s app. Tap \"Edit plan\" to change it.</string>

    <string name="info_cpu_title">About CPU Load</string>
    <string name="info_cpu_body">Total CPU usage across all apps. Since Android 8, this number is only available to system apps — so most phones show it as unavailable. We use a best-effort estimate when the device happens to allow it.</string>


